Print CPU exceptions unconditionally on the console.

The added console_out_f() in exception_debug() sits outside the
#ifdef DEBUGGER / exception_debugging guard, so exceptions are shown even
with the debugger off. (Amiberry's exception-breakpoint message in
debug_exception() already uses console_out_f(), so that half of the FS-UAE
patch needs no port.)

Index: demoscene-toolchain/submodules/amiberry/src/newcpu.cpp
===================================================================
--- demoscene-toolchain.orig/submodules/amiberry/src/newcpu.cpp
+++ demoscene-toolchain/submodules/amiberry/src/newcpu.cpp
@@ -2591,6 +2591,7 @@ static void exception_debug (int nr)
 		return;
 	console_out_f (_T("Exception %d, PC=%08X\n"), nr, M68K_GETPC);
 #endif
+	console_out_f (_T("Exception %d, PC=%08X\n"), nr, M68K_GETPC);
 }
 
 #ifdef CPUEMU_13
